#4471 was merged as one issue ("dates parse mm/dd in eu locales"). It holds **three** problems.
The export has 427 rows but **412 reports**: 15 rows came twice. We count one report per id.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Three issues, three fixes. Fixing the parser alone leaves 38 of the 412 reports open.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is computed from the data. It files the 5 one-day reports under `parser` (379), because
it looks only at tenant and channel. The three problems, as the desk counts them:

| # | Problem | Reports | Who |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Parser** reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates | 379 (5 of them are also problem 3) | all 11 tenants, app, email and form |
| 2 | **Form hint**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so people at day-first tenants type month first | 33 | alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour (form) |
| 3 | **One day off**: a date lands exactly one day away, not a month/day swap. Looks like a time zone or day-boundary bug | 5 | R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620 |

379 + 33 = 412. The desk counts a report where it is filed, so the 5 one-day reports sit in the parser's 379 and also form problem 3.

## Why the merge hid this

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. All three problems share subjects such as "Wrong day on the invite".
- Intake tags from the browser. It tagged 15 of the 33 hint reports as `parser`.
- The 5 one-day reports say what they are in the body: "one day off", "arrived before I made the booking", "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday".

## What to do

- Fix the parser (#4471 keeps this one).
- Change the booking-v3 hint for day-first tenants, or make the form read what it prints.
- Open a time-zone investigation for the 5 one-day reports.
- Replace decision 0001 with a new record. An accepted decision is never edited.

